{
  "version": "agentcompute.executor-protocol/v0",
  "verifiedAgainst": "AgentDevice 5ea20669f2d8 (main), 2026-11-03",
  "notes": [
    "servers.host: the tools the built-in `host` MCP server (agentrouter mcp-serve host, crates/connector-cli/src/host/mod.rs:52-66) answers in tools/list, in that order; `name` is what the host server registers, `wireName` is what the aggregator exposes on the link (`<server>__<tool>`, crates/aggregator/src/lib.rs:1332)",
    "readOnly = annotations.readOnlyHint (crates/connector-cli/src/host/mod.rs:45-50); destructiveHint = !readOnly; openWorldHint = (name == \"exec\"). Tools without readOnlyHint get a checkpoint before the call (HOSTD-MCP §7.2)",
    "inputSchema is copied from the json! literal in the cited source with Rust constants resolved to their values (e.g. CHUNK_MAX = 4194304, exec::TIMEOUT_MAX_MS / 1000 = 600)",
    "internal: tools whose name starts with `_`. The host server lists them, the aggregator drops them from its tools/list (crates/aggregator/src/servers.rs:766-772) but forwards a tools/call by name (crates/aggregator/src/lib.rs:1866-1930 has no list check); `_port_bridge` exists only on Unix (host/mod.rs:63-64)",
    "servers.link: the aggregator's reserved management tools (crates/aggregator/src/lib.rs:2272-2380); names only, no inputSchema copied",
    "hostd's own unit test pins the public host list and its readOnly flags: crates/connector-cli/src/host/mod.rs:601-646"
  ],
